The scene depicts a nighttime driving scenario with wet road conditions and fog, leading to multiple safety risks. The RDF triples strictly adhere to the provided ontology vocabulary. Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimeWetRoadDriving" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasObstacle :roadObject1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 .

:roadObject1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Wet road surface with reflective sheen" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition, :RainyCondition .

:risk1 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Reduced traction due to wet road surface" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Limited visibility due to nighttime and rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision due to reduced visibility and slippery road" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.65"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.80"^^xsd:float .
```

